<LegalLayout title="Cookies Policy" description="Thornfell does not use cookies or tracking.">
    <h2>What cookies are</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small text files a website stores on your device. They let a site remember things about your visit, and they are often used to track people across the web.</p>

    <h2>Our position</h2>
    <p>This website does not set any cookies. We do not use analytics, advertising, social media or preference cookies, and the site works fully without them.</p>

    <h2>No tracking</h2>
    <p>We do not use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel or any other tracking service. Our fonts and images are served from our own website, so loading a page does not send your details to third parties such as Google.</p>

    <h2>Your browser settings</h2>
    <p>Because we do not use cookies, there is nothing you need to turn off on this site. If you want to block cookies on other websites, you can do so in your browser settings:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Chrome: Settings › Privacy and security › Third-party cookies</li>
        <li>Firefox: Settings › Privacy &amp; Security</li>
        <li>Safari: Settings › Privacy</li>
        <li>Edge: Settings › Cookies and site permissions</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we ever introduce cookies, for example when we add online payments, we will update this page and explain which cookies are used and why.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions about cookies on this site, <ContactLine />.</p>
</LegalLayout>
